3. RavynXHCIPort and RavynAHCIPort
----------------------------------

RavynAHCIPort is ravynOS's AHCI driver, written by Zoe Knox (ravynOS, April
2026). PureDarwin's changes to it went back to ravynOS in its pull request #561
(9 July 2026).

RavynXHCIPort is a USB (xHCI) host controller and mass storage driver written
for PureDarwin by Vali0004, starting from the structure of RavynAHCIPort. It
was added here on 10 July 2026 (ee1a459d3) and contributed to ravynOS two days
later, in its pull request #564 (12 July 2026). Its files keep the ravynOS
notice of the code it was derived from. It is PureDarwin's work, shared with
ravynOS, not a driver taken from ravynOS.


4. Forks and derived works
--------------------------

PureDarwin is open source and forks are welcome. This section has two parts,
and they are different in kind.

4a. What the licences require

What you must do depends on the licence of each file you take (section 1,
section 2 and the file's own notice), and on how you distribute it. In
summary, and only as a summary of those licences:

- Preserve copyright and licence notices, and provide licence texts, as
  required by each applicable licence.
- For files under MPL-2.0, when you distribute them or programs built from
  them, make the source of those files, including your changes to them,
  available under MPL-2.0 as that licence requires.
- Follow the terms of any third-party file as its own licence states them.

The licences themselves are what bind, not this summary. Renaming identifiers,
bundle names or paths does not change them.

4b. What the project asks

These go beyond the licences and are a request, not a legal condition. They are
how we would like PureDarwin's work to be represented:

- Keep every copyright notice, licence notice and SPDX line in the files you
  take, even where a licence would allow less.
- Say plainly, wherever you describe your system (READMEs, release notes,
  announcements and posts), that it is based on PureDarwin, and which of the
  features you show come from PureDarwin and which are new in your work.
- Name the PureDarwin revision you started from.
- Send fixes back upstream where you can. Pull requests are welcome
  (CONTRIBUTING.md).

The project's history is the record of who did what. Its git log is public at
https://github.com/PureDarwin/PureDarwin.
